.SH NAME
ssoosshd-nss-status - Show the daemon's state and check that this host consults it.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoosshd-nss status [flags] [args]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the directory connection's state (online, offline, unauthorized or rate limited), the server, the fleet key id, the cache counts and the last error, from the running daemon, with any group name collisions (a directory group with a local group's name and another gid, which is not resolved on this host) and refused groups (outside min_id..max_id) met since the start or the last SIGHUP; then whether nsswitch.conf lists systemd on its passwd, group and shadow lines, and whether nscd or unscd is running, which would cache a slow lookup's "not found". Exits non-zero when the daemon does not answer or a check fails.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for status


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--admin-socket\fP="/run/ssoossh-nss/admin.sock"
	the admin socket the CLI and the daemon share

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP="/etc/ssoossh/nss.yaml"
	the daemon's configuration file

.PP
\fB--overrides\fP="/etc/ssoossh/nss-overrides.yaml"
	the host override file


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBssoosshd-nss(8)\fP


